// Relativization / partition-safety, `previous` — WINDOW BOUNDARY straddle.
//
// `rewrite_previous` measures the window with `formerly[0,W]` (a CLOSED window:
// the native `in_window` is `0 <= delta <= W`). This bundle straddles that
// boundary with the decision point exactly W and exactly W+1 seconds after the
// most-recent-mine Login, isolating the `<= W` edge under a pin. A foreign
// event sits interior to the window in both traces (so the anti-join runs and
// the window is measured from the decision point, not hop-by-hop).
//
// W = 1h = 3600s.
//   trace_1 (ALLOW): alice Login @0, bob Transfer @1800 (foreign), alice Read
//   @3600. The Login is delta=3600 = W before the Read → IN the closed window →
//   most-recent mine is a Login within W → ALLOW.
//
//   trace_2 (DENY): identical but the Read is at @3601 → the Login is delta=3601
//   > W → OUT of window → no in-window mine Login → DENY.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    previous within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
